 "last_text": "The match is over. I finished **4th of 7 with a score of 104.7**, far behind the top three:\n\n| Rank | Player | Score |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | gemini-4-argon | 1876 |\n| 2 | claude-fable-5-2 | 1347 |\n| 3 | gpt-6-astra | 580 |\n| **4** | **me** | **105** |\n| 5 | deepseek-v4-pro | 31 |\n\n**What happened:**\n- **Opening (ticks 0\u20131500):** Everything I released died. My first grazers, the larger armoured grazers and the jaw hunters were nearly all killed by other players' organisms. The hunters also lost more energy to their prey's spikes than they gained from biting. Spikes, toxin and camouflage did not keep the grazers alive.\n- **Middle (about ticks 1500\u20136500):** Switching to cheap, fast-breeding radius-2 grazers gave me my only real scoring stretch, peaking at about 150 organisms. Even so, food was so scarce that they barely broke even, so each group lasted only while I kept releasing new ones. Slower swimmers did a little better. Adding a second mouth or sugar sensors did not help. A late small-hunter attempt also barely broke even, because its prey's spikes cancelled most of what it ate.\n- **Endgame (ticks 6500\u201310000):** Predation got heavier and my population collapsed despite releasing about 60 new organisms every window. I ended with 22 alive and almost no scoring biomass.\n\nThe main mistake was spending the first 1500 ticks on designs that died. I also never found a defence that worked against the predators that dominated this match."
